config NVME_MDEV_VFIO
	tristate "NVMe mediated VFIO virtual controller (EXPERIMENTAL)"
	depends on BLOCK && VFIO && 64BIT
	select VFIO_MDEV
	select VHOST_TASK
	select BLK_DMA_PREMAP
	help
	  Exposes host block devices (e.g. NVMe namespaces or partitions of
	  them) to a guest as the namespaces of a virtual NVMe PCIe
	  controller, using a VFIO mediated device.  The guest uses its own,
	  unmodified NVMe driver; a polling thread, which belongs to the
	  process using the device (QEMU), translates the I/O commands and
	  sends them through the block layer, as polled bios to devices that
	  can poll (configure poll queues on NVMe devices, nvme.poll_queues).

	  If unsure, say N.
